# 26. FINANCIAL DATA INTEGRITY

This is a critical requirement.

Implement reliable accounting rules.

1. Every financial transaction must have a clear type.
2. Transfers must not inflate income or expenses.
3. Investment purchases must not be counted as household consumption expenses in net worth calculations.
4. Loan repayments must distinguish principal and interest.
5. Asset purchases must not cause duplicate asset accounting.
6. Credit card purchases and repayments must not be double counted.
7. Joint assets must respect ownership percentages.
8. Savings goals must not be counted as additional assets on top of their underlying bank balances.
9. Account balances must reconcile with transaction history.
10. Historical records must remain auditable.

Define and document a consistent accounting model before implementing reports.

